1
00:00:05,831 --> 00:00:07,464
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:07,464 --> 00:00:09,031
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:10,331 --> 00:00:12,064
- So good, right?
- Can you finish it all?

4
00:00:12,131 --> 00:00:13,131
What is this?

5
00:00:15,831 --> 00:00:19,064
Fried meatballs? Looks good.

6
00:00:21,697 --> 00:00:23,213
I didn't order any for you, Dad.

7
00:00:24,431 --> 00:00:26,414
We can just share.

8
00:00:27,290 --> 00:00:28,677
There's none for you three either.

9
00:00:28,884 --> 00:00:30,417
I only ordered for Gyeol and me.

10
00:00:33,831 --> 00:00:36,364
From now on, do your own laundry,

11
00:00:36,697 --> 00:00:38,464
and fix your own meals.

12
00:00:39,564 --> 00:00:42,064
What? Are you screwing over your family?

13
00:00:43,031 --> 00:00:46,206
Eat whatever you want, all of you.

14
00:00:46,357 --> 00:00:49,601
As of today, I resign
as the eldest of this house.

15
00:00:51,717 --> 00:00:53,021
Gyeol.

16
00:00:58,564 --> 00:01:00,157
- Want some sweet and sour pork?
- Yes.

17
00:01:00,231 --> 00:01:01,264
"Resign."

18
00:01:03,301 --> 00:01:04,614
Is this a joke?

19
00:01:05,537 --> 00:01:08,107
It's good, isn't it?

20
00:01:09,003 --> 00:01:11,012
- The sweet and sour pork here is good.
- Did you do this?

21
00:01:11,331 --> 00:01:12,364
Are you kidding me?

22
00:01:14,204 --> 00:01:16,304
You're the only one here who picks fights.

23
00:01:16,377 --> 00:01:18,177
It must have been Dad.

24
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:19,877
What?

25
00:01:26,831 --> 00:01:28,531
- Mom.
- Yes?

26
00:01:28,831 --> 00:01:30,431
I feel like I'm in the way.

27
00:01:32,331 --> 00:01:36,931
It's okay. Pretend no one's here,
and just eat without worrying.

28
00:01:37,131 --> 00:01:39,664
Black bean noodles for once.
Tastes so good, doesn't it?

29
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:40,877
Yes.

30
00:01:46,664 --> 00:01:50,331
Who was it? Who pissed off
our oldest daughter like this?

31
00:01:51,164 --> 00:01:53,112
It's your fault, all of you.

32
00:01:53,164 --> 00:01:55,431
Grown adults, fighting like that?

33
00:01:55,831 --> 00:01:57,153
You're not children.

34
00:01:57,831 --> 00:02:01,910
Getting hauled to a police station?
Are you out of your minds?

35
00:02:02,631 --> 00:02:05,007
I don't think you're in a position
to say that, Dad.

36
00:02:05,131 --> 00:02:07,719
- Exactly.
- I'm the victim here.

37
00:02:07,931 --> 00:02:12,171
Some woman ditched me with the bill.
I just got played!

38
00:02:12,650 --> 00:02:13,908
Seeing another woman again?

39
00:02:14,251 --> 00:02:16,219
You're not one to talk either.

40
00:02:17,431 --> 00:02:21,593
A woman, yes, but not that kind.
She was just...

41
00:02:21,837 --> 00:02:24,637
She said she'd buy me tuna,
so I just went along.

42
00:02:25,131 --> 00:02:27,689
When is that man going to grow up?

43
00:02:28,050 --> 00:02:29,150
That man?

44
00:02:29,731 --> 00:02:32,506
First you kill me off and bring me back,

45
00:02:32,571 --> 00:02:34,371
and now I'm flat-out "that man?"

46
00:02:34,631 --> 00:02:38,933
Keep needling me like that
and I might show up at your wedding.

47
00:02:39,031 --> 00:02:41,639
I could wear
a "Han Gyu Yeong's Real Dad" name tag,

48
00:02:41,664 --> 00:02:44,453
and take the parents' seat!

49
00:02:45,006 --> 00:02:47,106
Han Gyu Rim, you deal with Dad.

50
00:02:47,131 --> 00:02:48,978
Just try coming to my wedding!

51
00:02:51,931 --> 00:02:56,609
Gyeol, sorry, but for a while at home,
how about we wear earbuds?

52
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:57,917
Why?

53
00:02:58,131 --> 00:03:02,186
What this family says isn't great
for your upbringing.

54
00:03:09,431 --> 00:03:12,034
It's okay, Mom. I tune it all out.

55
00:03:13,831 --> 00:03:15,666
- All done?
- Yes.

56
00:03:16,017 --> 00:03:19,272
Go brush your teeth
and do your homework. Up you go.

57
00:03:21,477 --> 00:03:22,477
Okay.

58
00:03:25,103 --> 00:03:27,733
- Thanks for the meal.
- Sure.

59
00:03:31,089 --> 00:03:32,578
I have something to tell you.

60
00:03:33,231 --> 00:03:34,831
Don't.

61
00:03:35,731 --> 00:03:37,433
You've been strange today.

62
00:03:37,631 --> 00:03:39,031
Completely strange.

63
00:03:39,331 --> 00:03:42,706
When you're this strange,
it's better to say nothing at all.

64
00:03:42,731 --> 00:03:44,131
I don't want to hear it.

65
00:03:44,164 --> 00:03:47,375
We have to be out of this house
in three months.

66
00:03:48,431 --> 00:03:49,976
What are you talking about now?

67
00:03:50,064 --> 00:03:53,031
The landlord wants us out.
We had it cheap for a long time.

68
00:03:53,197 --> 00:03:54,967
Isn't she just asking for more rent?

69
00:03:55,431 --> 00:03:58,205
No. She just wants us out, period.

70
00:03:58,951 --> 00:04:00,689
Then where are we supposed to live?

71
00:04:01,164 --> 00:04:03,086
Everyone figures that out for themselves.

72
00:04:05,231 --> 00:04:07,543
What do you mean, figure it out ourselves?

73
00:04:07,631 --> 00:04:09,237
Just find us a place yourself.

74
00:04:09,364 --> 00:04:11,463
I just need to be in Seoul.

75
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:15,965
Why do I have to do all of it?

76
00:04:17,964 --> 00:04:20,839
Because you're the eldest of this house.

77
00:04:20,864 --> 00:04:22,364
I already told you.

78
00:04:22,664 --> 00:04:24,831
That I resign as the eldest here.

79
00:04:25,731 --> 00:04:27,031
Is "eldest" an elected position?

80
00:04:27,131 --> 00:04:28,931
You can't just resign
because you feel like it.

81
00:04:28,964 --> 00:04:31,408
You're the one cutting yourself
out of this family. Zip it.

82
00:04:32,031 --> 00:04:34,078
What? Is something actually going on?

83
00:04:34,131 --> 00:04:37,982
We can't all live together
on the money we have anyway.

84
00:04:38,539 --> 00:04:44,833
Gyu Min and Gyu Seo are minors,
so until they're grown, they live with me.

85
00:04:45,031 --> 00:04:48,103
Gyu O and Dad, find your own places.

86
00:04:49,031 --> 00:04:51,767
I'm not taking questions.

87
00:04:55,231 --> 00:04:58,531
So the twins and Gyeol live with you,

88
00:04:58,531 --> 00:05:00,231
and I live with Gyu O?

89
00:05:00,231 --> 00:05:02,265
I'm not living with Dad.

90
00:05:03,239 --> 00:05:06,539
Hey, Gyu O won't live with me.
What am I supposed to do?

91
00:05:06,564 --> 00:05:08,750
You're dropping a lot of bombs today.

92
00:05:08,931 --> 00:05:11,806
Have you been taking classes?
Did someone give you lessons?

93
00:05:11,831 --> 00:05:14,531
Han Gyu Yeong, she said no questions.

94
00:05:14,631 --> 00:05:16,131
Han Gyu Rim isn't in her right mind.

95
00:05:16,164 --> 00:05:18,941
If I let this go, I'm the one
who gets stuck with the garbage.

96
00:05:20,798 --> 00:05:22,528
- Move.
- Hey.

97
00:05:22,637 --> 00:05:23,859
- Hey!
- Hey!

98
00:05:23,884 --> 00:05:25,317
- Hey!
- What!

99
00:05:25,431 --> 00:05:26,506
Hey, garbage?

100
00:05:26,531 --> 00:05:28,431
Is this family garbage to you?

101
00:05:28,431 --> 00:05:30,013
What, did you think you were pure gold?

102
00:05:30,198 --> 00:05:33,206
- Hey. Enough, Han Gyu Yeong.
- You stop her, Han Gyu O.

103
00:05:33,231 --> 00:05:37,764
Han Gyu Rim's a hardhead.
Once she snaps, nobody can stop her.

104
00:05:38,003 --> 00:05:40,732
Then you should have kept her
from snapping.

105
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:44,524
Why mess with someone
and cause all this trouble?

106
00:05:44,657 --> 00:05:47,108
You're one to talk about living right.

107
00:05:47,164 --> 00:05:50,456
You, asking for tuna?
You could've just had canned tuna.

108
00:05:50,864 --> 00:05:53,986
Did you pay for the tuna? Gyu Rim did.

109
00:05:54,204 --> 00:05:58,536
You never bought these kids a thing,
and now you're giving advice?

110
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:19,831
So it really was just yours and Gyeol's.

111
00:06:21,617 --> 00:06:23,517
Fine. I get it.

112
00:06:23,690 --> 00:06:26,723
With Dad, Gyu O, and Gyu Seo
bouncing in and out of police stations,

113
00:06:26,964 --> 00:06:29,431
it's easy to burn out and break down.

114
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:32,206
You're human. You can get tired.

115
00:06:32,231 --> 00:06:34,631
"Why is my life like this?"
Your self-esteem hits rock bottom.

116
00:06:34,864 --> 00:06:37,973
"What's the point of living like this?"
You can absolutely feel that way.

117
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:40,023
Your hard work? Your sacrifice?

118
00:06:40,264 --> 00:06:45,155
I get it, more than enough.
And sometimes I've felt sorry for you too.

119
00:06:46,164 --> 00:06:48,431
So just hold on a little longer.

120
00:06:48,671 --> 00:06:50,571
Once I marry and inherit,

121
00:06:50,631 --> 00:06:53,731
I'll pay you back in full
for everything you've been through...

122
00:06:53,731 --> 00:06:54,731
Get...

123
00:06:56,098 --> 00:06:57,298
lost.

124
00:06:57,397 --> 00:07:00,630
What? Get lost? Did you just say that?

125
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,431
I'm studying conversational English.

126
00:07:05,664 --> 00:07:06,764
Give me a break.

127
00:07:07,031 --> 00:07:08,831
You? Conversational English?

128
00:07:08,931 --> 00:07:11,064
They say confidence is the key
to speaking English.

129
00:07:11,331 --> 00:07:13,231
They say don't worry
about getting it wrong.

130
00:07:13,264 --> 00:07:15,864
Just say it with confidence.

131
00:07:16,043 --> 00:07:17,601
Get lost.

132
00:07:18,190 --> 00:07:20,791
You're not some rebellious teenager.
What are you doing?

133
00:07:21,064 --> 00:07:22,731
They say a sudden change means death.

134
00:07:22,756 --> 00:07:25,589
Exactly. The Han Gyu Rim you knew is dead.

135
00:07:30,331 --> 00:07:33,021
What is that...

136
00:07:33,524 --> 00:07:35,125
Has she lost her mind?

137
00:07:35,331 --> 00:07:37,331
Get lost?

138
00:07:37,811 --> 00:07:39,221
Give me a break.

139
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:49,777
Making sandwiches?

140
00:07:50,491 --> 00:07:52,868
Yes. Gyeol asked for them.

141
00:07:54,811 --> 00:07:56,096
Want some?

142
00:07:56,631 --> 00:07:59,390
No, you said it's every man for himself.

143
00:07:59,415 --> 00:08:00,915
I'll make my own.

144
00:08:01,331 --> 00:08:03,321
Gyu Seo said he'd handle his own too.

145
00:08:03,631 --> 00:08:04,931
Don't worry about us, Gyu Rim.

146
00:08:05,631 --> 00:08:07,922
- Sure, let's do that.
- Okay.

147
00:08:09,264 --> 00:08:10,431
You did well, Gyu Rim.

148
00:08:10,631 --> 00:08:12,431
You should have done this ages ago.

149
00:08:15,635 --> 00:08:17,321
Gyeol's going to love this.

150
00:08:20,017 --> 00:08:24,291
I saw on TV that sea squirts
are in season right now.

151
00:08:26,404 --> 00:08:30,640
Gyu Rim, should we make
soybean paste stew with sea squirts?

152
00:08:31,531 --> 00:08:32,668
Make it yourself.

153
00:08:34,084 --> 00:08:37,973
The paste and veggies are in the fridge,
and the store sells sea squirts.

154
00:08:41,643 --> 00:08:43,654
The kids, I can understand,

155
00:08:44,964 --> 00:08:46,997
but shouldn't you cut me some slack?

156
00:08:48,177 --> 00:08:50,836
I'm your father.
You're supposed to take care of me.

157
00:08:51,710 --> 00:08:53,910
Do you want a sandwich then, Dad?

158
00:08:54,504 --> 00:08:56,980
I don't eat sandwiches in the morning.

159
00:08:57,584 --> 00:09:00,284
Make me soybean paste stew,
with sea squirts in it.

160
00:09:01,031 --> 00:09:02,748
I don't want to make stew.

161
00:09:03,064 --> 00:09:05,648
And I don't like sea squirts.

162
00:09:10,231 --> 00:09:12,814
Han Gyeol, are you ready for school?

163
00:09:15,831 --> 00:09:17,506
Let's eat our sandwiches.

164
00:09:23,731 --> 00:09:27,798
Hey, is that really your sister, Gyu Rim?

165
00:09:28,337 --> 00:09:32,537
Big news. My sister suddenly
got seriously cool.

166
00:09:32,564 --> 00:09:35,678
- What's with you now?
- What?

167
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:23,097
Hey, what is all this?

168
00:10:23,131 --> 00:10:24,464
You haven't eaten yet, right?

169
00:10:24,931 --> 00:10:27,591
I went to the fish market,
and they had some beautiful croaker.

170
00:10:29,175 --> 00:10:30,306
But here's the thing.

171
00:10:30,331 --> 00:10:32,664
Seo Hyeon left at dawn
to prep for a meeting.

172
00:10:32,784 --> 00:10:35,046
I brought it for you and your wife, sir.

173
00:10:37,317 --> 00:10:38,883
Where did your wife go?

174
00:10:38,964 --> 00:10:42,885
Yes, she went to buy dried pollack
to make me hangover soup.

175
00:10:43,484 --> 00:10:45,251
I heard she likes croaker.

176
00:10:45,643 --> 00:10:48,910
I'll slice it up now and make
a stew and pancakes too.

177
00:10:49,737 --> 00:10:52,424
Sure. Hey, Mu Jin.

178
00:10:53,131 --> 00:10:56,808
I love that you're coming in this hard,

179
00:10:57,624 --> 00:11:02,197
I just don't know
if Yun Hui will be moved.

180
00:11:02,806 --> 00:11:07,006
It's fine. I'd just be happy
if you enjoyed it.

181
00:11:07,031 --> 00:11:09,966
Sure. You're the bigger man.

182
00:11:10,131 --> 00:11:11,131
Anything I can help with?

183
00:11:11,164 --> 00:11:13,424
No. I brought my own knife and board,

184
00:11:13,464 --> 00:11:15,731
so don't worry about it,
and just have a seat.

185
00:11:15,731 --> 00:11:17,131
Sure, shall I?

186
00:11:18,664 --> 00:11:19,964
That must be Yun Hui.

187
00:11:20,531 --> 00:11:21,775
I'm in here.

188
00:11:21,864 --> 00:11:23,831
- Yes, I'm home.
- Yes.

189
00:11:26,904 --> 00:11:27,971
Hello, ma'am.

190
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:34,700
Mu Jin brought croaker
because he knows you like it.

191
00:11:34,725 --> 00:11:37,910
And our chef here is cooking it all today.

192
00:11:39,931 --> 00:11:41,445
So I'm a joke to you.

193
00:11:42,958 --> 00:11:43,991
Yun Hui.

194
00:11:44,431 --> 00:11:46,231
The effort you said you'd make...

195
00:11:47,364 --> 00:11:50,993
was being this rude
and putting people on the spot?

196
00:11:53,570 --> 00:11:56,070
Since when is effort
this pushy and selfish?

197
00:11:56,144 --> 00:11:57,144
Honey.

198
00:11:58,631 --> 00:12:01,531
I'm sorry if I made things
uncomfortable for you.

199
00:12:02,490 --> 00:12:04,677
If you know that, don't do it again.

200
00:12:12,831 --> 00:12:14,608
I feel terrible about this.

201
00:12:16,196 --> 00:12:18,885
No, sir. I should have thought it through.

202
00:12:20,364 --> 00:12:22,206
I'll leave the croaker here.

203
00:12:22,297 --> 00:12:25,030
She's a great cook,
so I hope you enjoy the fish.

204
00:12:25,831 --> 00:12:27,164
- Mu Jin.
- Yes.

205
00:12:27,864 --> 00:12:30,051
You won't stop coming by, will you?

206
00:12:30,464 --> 00:12:33,015
Never. I'll be back soon.

207
00:12:33,197 --> 00:12:36,130
Just open the door for me again, then.

208
00:12:36,764 --> 00:12:39,131
Sure. Thank you for the croaker.

209
00:13:11,297 --> 00:13:12,588
Mu Jin left.

210
00:13:15,331 --> 00:13:21,408
Honey, you being this dead set
against it...

211
00:13:22,031 --> 00:13:25,564
means there's more to it
than Mu Jin giving Seo Hyeon a hard time.

212
00:13:26,243 --> 00:13:28,976
Something serious...

213
00:13:31,731 --> 00:13:33,531
Can't you tell me what it is?

214
00:13:36,231 --> 00:13:38,670
Did you hear something somewhere?

215
00:13:38,695 --> 00:13:43,438
Like Mu Jin having a terrible illness,
something like that.

216
00:13:45,131 --> 00:13:46,431
I'll get dinner ready.

217
00:13:47,064 --> 00:13:48,131
Honey.

218
00:13:49,110 --> 00:13:51,119
What, is he a gambler?

219
00:13:52,164 --> 00:13:53,964
Or the world's worst womanizer?

220
00:13:54,117 --> 00:13:57,150
Does he have more than one woman
hidden away, something like that?

221
00:13:57,557 --> 00:13:58,955
It's nothing like that.

222
00:13:59,931 --> 00:14:03,638
I need something I can understand
before I can take your side.

223
00:14:08,071 --> 00:14:10,070
I'm sorry. This is all because of me.

224
00:14:11,897 --> 00:14:13,798
That's not what I'm asking.

225
00:14:14,110 --> 00:14:18,677
I'm saying I want to understand you.

226
00:14:24,131 --> 00:14:26,164
You can't understand me.

227
00:14:35,531 --> 00:14:37,795
- What?
- Hey. Move aside, you brat.

228
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:39,639
Are you moving or not?

229
00:14:39,664 --> 00:14:41,464
Move it right now, you jerk.

230
00:14:41,931 --> 00:14:44,131
I told you, sign the pledge.

231
00:14:45,564 --> 00:14:48,563
Sign a pledge that you'll never
give Gyu Rim a hard time again.

232
00:14:49,164 --> 00:14:51,052
How am I giving her a hard time?

233
00:14:51,663 --> 00:14:56,355
Gyu Rim went and told on me
to you already, did she?

234
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:58,577
Gyu Rim never told on you.

235
00:14:59,331 --> 00:15:01,006
Word's gotten around the whole arcade,

236
00:15:01,031 --> 00:15:03,931
that you're giving Gyu Rim a hard time,
making her do all the hard work,

237
00:15:03,931 --> 00:15:05,760
and trying to kick her out.

238
00:15:07,638 --> 00:15:09,931
I'm nowhere near done.

239
00:15:10,431 --> 00:15:14,433
Is that enough for the schemer
who played my precious son?

240
00:15:14,731 --> 00:15:16,145
This is just the beginning.

241
00:15:16,344 --> 00:15:18,544
I haven't done a tenth of it.

242
00:15:18,643 --> 00:15:23,110
How many times do I have to say it?
I dumped her, she didn't dump me.

243
00:15:24,064 --> 00:15:28,231
Sure. And pigs fly.

244
00:15:28,731 --> 00:15:33,340
If I had my way, I'd rip every hair
out of her head and still want more.

245
00:15:35,831 --> 00:15:39,288
Just try touching one hair
on Gyu Rim's head.

246
00:15:39,369 --> 00:15:42,665
I'll get ten degrees crazier
for every hair.

247
00:15:43,364 --> 00:15:45,064
You know what happens
when I go off the rails?

248
00:15:45,964 --> 00:15:50,031
You spineless, brainless brat.

249
00:15:50,531 --> 00:15:53,064
Give me back my phone and move, you punk.

250
00:15:53,064 --> 00:15:56,031
What, so you can call Gyu Rim
and curse her out?

251
00:15:56,031 --> 00:15:58,306
- That's right.
- Until you sign that pledge...

252
00:15:58,331 --> 00:16:00,931
you're not getting your phone
and I'm not moving.

253
00:16:05,964 --> 00:16:09,543
- Yes, where are you? Almost here?
- Yes, I'm outside.

254
00:16:09,716 --> 00:16:12,031
Let go, you brat. You punk.

255
00:16:12,131 --> 00:16:14,131
- Let go.
- Sit down already.

256
00:16:15,631 --> 00:16:16,764
I'm here.

257
00:16:17,564 --> 00:16:19,918
You're the only one free at this hour.

258
00:16:20,164 --> 00:16:22,131
Keep an eye on this old lady for me.

259
00:16:22,831 --> 00:16:23,831
Why?

260
00:16:24,064 --> 00:16:26,256
That punk won't let me move a muscle,

261
00:16:26,431 --> 00:16:29,928
afraid I'll go after Han Gyu Rim.

262
00:16:30,131 --> 00:16:32,506
Why is she giving my sister a hard time?

263
00:16:32,531 --> 00:16:35,864
Ask her when you're alone with her.
Just make sure she doesn't leave.

264
00:16:36,231 --> 00:16:38,470
If she goes out, your sister's in trouble.

265
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:41,864
Keep her here until she signs the pledge.
Got it?

266
00:16:42,097 --> 00:16:43,097
Yes.

267
00:16:44,864 --> 00:16:47,206
Hey, give me my phone back.

268
00:16:47,231 --> 00:16:49,231
I hope you trip on your way out.

269
00:16:49,431 --> 00:16:51,831
That punk. I'm worn out.

270
00:16:51,831 --> 00:16:58,831
(Suragan Side Dishes)

271
00:16:59,664 --> 00:17:01,731
That old woman, honestly.

272
00:17:07,864 --> 00:17:10,428
- Welcome. Heung Sik.
- Gyu Rim.

273
00:17:12,431 --> 00:17:14,206
Is Su Nam all right?

274
00:17:14,231 --> 00:17:15,664
Her phone was off too.

275
00:17:16,031 --> 00:17:17,531
She turned it off so she could sleep.

276
00:17:17,831 --> 00:17:21,591
It's just an upset stomach. They said
she'll be fine with rest and medicine.

277
00:17:22,931 --> 00:17:25,258
It's not because of me, is it?

278
00:17:25,464 --> 00:17:29,820
No, she gets more energetic
when she's angry.

279
00:17:30,377 --> 00:17:33,477
But why are you here instead of with her?

280
00:17:34,031 --> 00:17:39,631
Well, she told me to come
help you out in her place.

281
00:17:39,750 --> 00:17:42,915
Look at this. It's too much
for one person.

282
00:17:43,364 --> 00:17:45,364
No, it's fine. I can handle it...

283
00:17:48,064 --> 00:17:52,331
Actually, would you? I could use a hand
with all these orders today.

284
00:17:52,331 --> 00:17:53,731
See? I knew it.

285
00:17:54,064 --> 00:17:58,277
I'll do anything, so put me
to work wherever you need.

286
00:18:07,711 --> 00:18:10,497
Today's deliveries go to...

287
00:18:10,804 --> 00:18:14,224
- Dajeong Apartments Complex 3, and...
- That's strange.

288
00:18:14,431 --> 00:18:15,606
What is it?

289
00:18:15,631 --> 00:18:20,464
Look me dead in the eye,
like you're trying to bore through it.

290
00:18:22,354 --> 00:18:23,584
Like this?

291
00:18:27,428 --> 00:18:28,764
I'm fine.

292
00:18:29,564 --> 00:18:33,294
My heart's barely racing.
Much better than yesterday.

293
00:18:33,831 --> 00:18:36,776
Keep this up, and I'll be able
to look at you like a piece of furniture.

294
00:18:38,191 --> 00:18:40,190
Should I keep looking at you then?

295
00:18:40,431 --> 00:18:43,276
No. Get back to work.

296
00:18:45,331 --> 00:18:48,580
Whatever Su Nam says, stay out of it.

297
00:18:48,844 --> 00:18:51,744
Let me handle my own problems, Heung Sik.

298
00:18:51,991 --> 00:18:53,291
That's how you help me.

299
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:56,486
Of course, I won't do a thing.

300
00:18:56,631 --> 00:18:58,464
You already did something, I think...

301
00:18:59,031 --> 00:19:01,790
You didn't lock her in the house, did you?

302
00:19:01,864 --> 00:19:03,085
Because she might come after me?

303
00:19:03,331 --> 00:19:06,231
No, never.

304
00:19:07,411 --> 00:19:08,837
Get to work.

305
00:19:10,064 --> 00:19:11,331
Something's off.

306
00:19:14,170 --> 00:19:16,370
Why can't I understand you?

307
00:19:17,831 --> 00:19:20,653
Why would I never be able
to understand you?

308
00:19:24,164 --> 00:19:26,516
What am I missing?

309
00:19:36,431 --> 00:19:37,531
Chairman Jang!

310
00:19:39,531 --> 00:19:40,531
Jang Hun Tae!

311
00:19:49,631 --> 00:19:52,839
His meeting with the chancellor ran long.
He'll be here soon.

312
00:19:54,364 --> 00:19:56,849
I didn't know Professor Cha
invited you too.

313
00:19:57,664 --> 00:19:59,331
Cha Yeong Su and I are closer.

314
00:19:59,431 --> 00:20:00,731
I know you're close.

315
00:20:01,731 --> 00:20:05,313
If we're counting closeness,
he and I go back to elementary school.

316
00:20:05,831 --> 00:20:07,479
We go back to kindergarten.

317
00:20:08,331 --> 00:20:10,639
Really? I didn't know.

318
00:20:15,164 --> 00:20:19,531
Did you tell Cha Yeong Su about our kids?

319
00:20:20,431 --> 00:20:21,637
Am I crazy?

320
00:20:21,664 --> 00:20:23,864
Right? Then why invite us together?

321
00:20:23,950 --> 00:20:25,390
I...

322
00:20:27,257 --> 00:20:30,182
didn't want to see you for a while.

323
00:20:32,231 --> 00:20:35,249
What is wrong with your wife?

324
00:20:35,531 --> 00:20:39,134
Who is she to reject him and give
someone else's fine son a hard time?

325
00:20:39,331 --> 00:20:43,036
Keep testing my patience,
and I'll do something about it.

326
00:20:43,311 --> 00:20:44,751
So what should I do?

327
00:20:45,364 --> 00:20:47,007
Should I get on my knees?

328
00:20:49,564 --> 00:20:51,562
You'd actually do it if I said so?

329
00:20:52,831 --> 00:20:54,099
If you say kneel, I kneel.

330
00:20:55,131 --> 00:20:57,130
- Kneel, then.
- I will.

331
00:20:58,631 --> 00:21:03,194
Hey, get up.

332
00:21:04,131 --> 00:21:06,931
Why are you kneeling?
Your wife should be the one kneeling.

333
00:21:06,964 --> 00:21:09,786
I've got nothing against you.
I've got plenty against your wife.

334
00:21:09,831 --> 00:21:11,961
That's the problem.

335
00:21:12,231 --> 00:21:13,806
A husband and wife are one.

336
00:21:13,831 --> 00:21:15,631
I'm my wife, and my wife is me.

337
00:21:15,731 --> 00:21:17,531
So for my sake, let it go.

338
00:21:19,764 --> 00:21:22,413
It's a sad life without a husband,
isn't it?

339
00:21:23,931 --> 00:21:25,031
Just be patient a little longer.

340
00:21:28,031 --> 00:21:30,631
That punk Yeong Su brings
two busy chairmen here,

341
00:21:30,631 --> 00:21:31,907
then disappears on us...

342
00:21:32,131 --> 00:21:34,931
- I'm leaving.
- Just wait. Rein in that temper.

343
00:21:35,064 --> 00:21:36,564
You won't age gracefully like that.

344
00:21:36,723 --> 00:21:39,560
- I'm aging plenty gracefully.
- Is that so?

345
00:21:39,964 --> 00:21:44,093
Some people think I'm
ten years younger than I am.

346
00:21:45,764 --> 00:21:46,864
Really?

347
00:21:47,031 --> 00:21:49,164
That's laying it on thick.

348
00:21:50,164 --> 00:21:51,231
It's a man, isn't it?

349
00:21:52,223 --> 00:21:54,800
- It's not a woman.
- Right.

350
00:21:55,764 --> 00:21:57,231
Watch out for con artists.

351
00:21:58,464 --> 00:22:00,039
Of course, Chairwoman Hong...

352
00:22:00,064 --> 00:22:03,331
you can spot a con artist
who's only after your money, right?

353
00:22:04,197 --> 00:22:06,407
- Please enjoy.
- Yes.

354
00:22:11,464 --> 00:22:12,464
Yes.

355
00:22:12,931 --> 00:22:15,731
Go ahead and eat. I'll take this call.

356
00:22:15,764 --> 00:22:17,848
- Yes, ma'am.
- Okay.

357
00:22:21,957 --> 00:22:23,505
I'm the one who pulled a con.

358
00:22:26,357 --> 00:22:29,211
I said I'd buy him tuna and then...

359
00:22:30,031 --> 00:22:32,134
What is wrong with me lately, Hun Tae?

360
00:22:32,483 --> 00:22:35,153
I think I'm losing it.
What am I going to do?

361
00:22:35,564 --> 00:22:37,088
Hey, what's this about tuna?

362
00:22:50,131 --> 00:22:51,666
Do you know any cults?

363
00:22:52,131 --> 00:22:53,606
Or any other weird religious groups?

364
00:22:54,531 --> 00:22:57,285
My Gyu Rim suddenly turned strange.

365
00:22:57,931 --> 00:23:00,006
You know how documentaries say...

366
00:23:00,031 --> 00:23:04,183
when someone falls for a cult,
they're told to cut off family first.

367
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:07,333
Our eldest, she...

368
00:23:10,370 --> 00:23:12,870
My eldest only cares about her family.

369
00:23:14,064 --> 00:23:17,388
I'm going to tail her first.

370
00:23:18,031 --> 00:23:19,202
Yes, got it.

371
00:23:19,931 --> 00:23:22,864
I'll call you when I know more.

372
00:23:23,817 --> 00:23:25,841
Sir, I'm truly sorry.

373
00:23:25,984 --> 00:23:28,405
Something urgent came up...

374
00:23:28,430 --> 00:23:32,434
I completely forgot you were
in that room eating tuna.

375
00:23:34,064 --> 00:23:35,231
It's fine.

376
00:23:35,964 --> 00:23:38,231
I guess I don't leave
much of an impression.

377
00:23:38,331 --> 00:23:40,131
It's not you, it's me.

378
00:23:40,131 --> 00:23:43,104
I've been terribly forgetful lately.

379
00:23:43,177 --> 00:23:47,046
Someone I know says people claim
forgetfulness when they've got no excuse.

380
00:23:47,731 --> 00:23:48,831
Well...

381
00:23:50,631 --> 00:23:53,364
I'll pay for last time.

382
00:23:53,831 --> 00:23:57,538
And I'd like to buy you tuna again
as an apology.

383
00:23:58,431 --> 00:24:02,078
No thanks. Just hearing the word tuna
sets me off now.

384
00:24:05,234 --> 00:24:06,541
In a bit.

385
00:24:10,834 --> 00:24:14,073
Then I'll buy you something
better than tuna.

386
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:18,512
What's better than tuna in this world?

387
00:24:20,014 --> 00:24:22,400
I find premium grouper better than tuna.

388
00:24:24,654 --> 00:24:26,197
Have you ever had true grouper?

389
00:24:27,271 --> 00:24:28,841
It was probably a knockoff.

390
00:24:29,514 --> 00:24:31,187
I mean the real thing,

391
00:24:31,314 --> 00:24:33,034
not leopard grouper.

392
00:24:33,514 --> 00:24:36,439
Did you run a sashimi place?
You know leopard grouper?

393
00:24:38,566 --> 00:24:40,779
You're clearly not just anybody.

394
00:24:41,687 --> 00:24:43,994
I ran a sashimi place for a while.

395
00:24:44,261 --> 00:24:48,827
Anyway, I'll buy you real grouper,
so forget the tuna.

396
00:24:50,674 --> 00:24:52,720
Do you know what grouper costs?

397
00:24:53,021 --> 00:24:56,027
It's whatever they ask for.

398
00:24:56,061 --> 00:24:58,001
I told you my savings club paid out.

399
00:25:00,401 --> 00:25:03,060
This time I really won't disappear.

400
00:25:03,061 --> 00:25:05,194
If you don't believe me,
I'll pay in advance.

401
00:25:05,811 --> 00:25:08,154
It's fine. Just eat your noodles.

402
00:25:08,901 --> 00:25:10,278
Sir.

403
00:25:12,041 --> 00:25:13,487
If I eat grouper,

404
00:25:14,781 --> 00:25:16,494
I'm afraid I'll cry.

405
00:25:17,994 --> 00:25:19,820
It'd bring back my shining days,

406
00:25:19,987 --> 00:25:21,760
when I ate tuna like it was kimchi,

407
00:25:22,567 --> 00:25:26,099
and how I threw those days away,

408
00:25:26,628 --> 00:25:28,747
with all the mistakes I made...

409
00:25:36,567 --> 00:25:38,767
If you're sorry, buy me
braised carp sometime.

410
00:25:49,753 --> 00:25:50,913
Ready to order?

411
00:25:54,011 --> 00:25:55,116
Yes, over here.

412
00:25:57,746 --> 00:26:00,486
Mu Jin came to my house?

413
00:26:02,752 --> 00:26:06,539
He got your mother
her absolute favorite, croaker,

414
00:26:07,831 --> 00:26:09,774
a fish this big,

415
00:26:09,799 --> 00:26:12,381
and even brought all the tools
to cook it himself,

416
00:26:13,436 --> 00:26:14,639
and failed.

417
00:26:17,546 --> 00:26:18,760
This won't work.

418
00:26:19,891 --> 00:26:22,547
I'm just going to register the marriage.

419
00:26:22,572 --> 00:26:24,965
You can register a marriage alone?

420
00:26:25,904 --> 00:26:27,286
Would Mu Jin even do it?

421
00:26:29,927 --> 00:26:32,464
What is wrong with my mother?

422
00:26:34,054 --> 00:26:35,058
Right.

423
00:26:35,333 --> 00:26:37,503
I figured she'd just vent and let it go,

424
00:26:37,997 --> 00:26:40,740
but I don't get it either.
That angel is usually so gentle.

425
00:26:40,861 --> 00:26:41,988
So I...

426
00:26:42,013 --> 00:26:46,121
ran through thousands of scenarios
asking why my mother is like this.

427
00:26:46,606 --> 00:26:50,967
And there's one thing I suspect.

428
00:26:52,607 --> 00:26:54,343
- Me too.
- You too?

429
00:26:55,984 --> 00:26:56,984
What is it?

430
00:27:01,347 --> 00:27:02,447
You first.

431
00:27:09,066 --> 00:27:12,098
My dad and Mu Jin's mother,

432
00:27:12,386 --> 00:27:14,760
they weren't just friends.
They dated, back in the day.

433
00:27:15,507 --> 00:27:17,707
And my mother recently found out.

434
00:27:18,022 --> 00:27:20,674
No way. Jinx.

435
00:27:21,420 --> 00:27:22,587
It can't be.

436
00:27:23,334 --> 00:27:26,662
You and I have both seen "no way"
come true plenty of times.

437
00:27:27,340 --> 00:27:28,840
Then what am I supposed to do?

438
00:27:30,513 --> 00:27:33,922
- You should break up.
- No. Why should I?

439
00:27:36,787 --> 00:27:38,734
You know how far my mind went?

440
00:27:42,008 --> 00:27:48,054
Maybe Mu Jin's father
is actually your father.

441
00:27:48,587 --> 00:27:49,634
Are you insane?

442
00:27:50,527 --> 00:27:52,667
Mu Jin's mother,
the chairwoman, said so herself.

443
00:27:52,913 --> 00:27:55,771
She said Mu Jin acts
just like Chairman Jang,

444
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,260
like they could be father and son.

445
00:27:58,441 --> 00:28:00,747
Are you crazy?
You think you can just say anything?

446
00:28:01,027 --> 00:28:03,400
Who are you playing games with right now?

447
00:28:03,601 --> 00:28:06,271
What do you even think of my father?

448
00:28:06,273 --> 00:28:07,467
Are you out of your mind, Park Jeong Woo?

449
00:28:10,047 --> 00:28:11,971
Let me see you again,

450
00:28:11,996 --> 00:28:13,859
and I'll kill you.

451
00:28:21,967 --> 00:28:23,427
I went way too far.

452
00:28:25,327 --> 00:28:26,634
Damn my imagination.

453
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:32,534
That hurts. She's got quite a punch.

454
00:28:36,630 --> 00:28:37,924
(Seo Hyeon's Mother)

455
00:28:41,480 --> 00:28:45,140
- Yes, ma'am.
- I'm calling to ask a favor, Jeong Woo.

456
00:28:46,557 --> 00:28:50,514
Keep this a secret between us.

457
00:28:52,434 --> 00:28:54,360
The girl Mu Jin dated,

458
00:28:55,841 --> 00:28:57,354
was her name Han Gyu Rim?

459
00:28:59,295 --> 00:29:02,687
Where can I find her?

460
00:29:03,334 --> 00:29:07,807
Braised potatoes, young radish kimchi,
and mung bean pancakes?

461
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:12,301
Our spicy beef soup came out great
this time. Would you like some?

462
00:29:14,627 --> 00:29:16,370
The seasoning this time...

463
00:29:21,339 --> 00:29:23,850
Would you like some of those
braised soybeans on the house?

464
00:29:24,621 --> 00:29:25,813
No need.

465
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:29,544
She doesn't flinch
no matter how my mother hounds her.

466
00:29:29,596 --> 00:29:31,528
Yes, thank you.

467
00:29:31,702 --> 00:29:34,234
Then, including the braised soybeans...

468
00:29:34,236 --> 00:29:35,801
Just like you wanted,

469
00:29:36,142 --> 00:29:38,278
I won't help you with a single thing,

470
00:29:38,778 --> 00:29:41,013
so get through all of it yourself,
Han Gyu Rim.

471
00:29:45,685 --> 00:29:46,814
(Gyu O)

472
00:29:47,754 --> 00:29:49,019
Hello, Gyu O.

473
00:29:49,021 --> 00:29:50,547
I'm on my way back from a delivery.

474
00:29:50,667 --> 00:29:51,972
Is the old lady behaving?

475
00:29:53,780 --> 00:29:55,640
Right, that's tough, isn't it?

476
00:29:56,007 --> 00:29:57,527
I'll head over now,

477
00:29:57,581 --> 00:29:58,740
hold on, I've got another call.

478
00:29:59,955 --> 00:30:01,981
What's this brat calling for?

479
00:30:03,938 --> 00:30:07,340
Gyu O, Gyu Yeong's calling.
I'll call you back.

480
00:30:13,708 --> 00:30:15,227
Did you hit the wrong number?

481
00:30:15,297 --> 00:30:18,381
Heung Sik, are you busy?

482
00:30:18,720 --> 00:30:20,219
Did you mean to call me?

483
00:30:20,894 --> 00:30:23,094
This is Heung Sik. Cho Heung Sik.

484
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,665
Has she lost it?

485
00:30:46,667 --> 00:30:50,934
I ordered you a vanilla latte,
figured you'd like something sweet.

486
00:30:52,787 --> 00:30:54,278
Are you sick?

487
00:30:55,047 --> 00:30:56,460
Did you check your temperature?

488
00:30:57,527 --> 00:30:59,400
This must feel strange coming from me.

489
00:30:59,494 --> 00:31:02,374
I get really sweet too
when I want something.

490
00:31:03,767 --> 00:31:05,374
What do you want from me?

491
00:31:08,274 --> 00:31:10,394
You know who Park Bun Rye is?

492
00:31:10,876 --> 00:31:13,727
My mother's legal name.

493
00:31:13,977 --> 00:31:17,174
Right. That's what I found when I looked.

494
00:31:17,921 --> 00:31:18,921
And?

495
00:31:20,521 --> 00:31:23,476
I pulled the property record,
and Park Bun Rye, I mean,

496
00:31:24,291 --> 00:31:26,981
Park Su Nam owns our house?

497
00:31:27,026 --> 00:31:28,209
So?

498
00:31:29,508 --> 00:31:33,034
Did you know she was trying
to kick my family out?

499
00:31:33,594 --> 00:31:34,598
What?

500
00:31:36,285 --> 00:31:37,416
That old woman, honestly.

501
00:31:39,170 --> 00:31:40,500
She told your family to move out?

502
00:31:41,881 --> 00:31:43,927
Gyu Rim broke it off with you, right?

503
00:31:43,941 --> 00:31:45,379
So your mother's getting revenge?

504
00:31:45,381 --> 00:31:47,907
We never dated. How could we break up?

505
00:31:48,881 --> 00:31:50,505
Go get Han Gyu Rim back.

506
00:31:50,507 --> 00:31:53,894
Tell her she gave you her body,
her heart, all of it. Take responsibility.

507
00:31:53,919 --> 00:31:54,919
What are you talking about?

508
00:31:55,596 --> 00:31:57,001
Gave me what?

509
00:31:57,601 --> 00:31:59,494
We haven't even held hands properly.

510
00:32:00,474 --> 00:32:01,883
What century did you come from...

511
00:32:01,963 --> 00:32:04,494
Never mind. Just cling to her.

512
00:32:04,547 --> 00:32:07,927
Say you can't live without her,
say you'll die. Threaten her.

513
00:32:07,952 --> 00:32:12,747
You made a whole scene telling me
to stay away from your sister.

514
00:32:14,181 --> 00:32:17,954
Back then I didn't know
Park Su Nam owned our house.

515
00:32:19,034 --> 00:32:21,798
Lean your head over here a second.

516
00:32:22,220 --> 00:32:23,714
I'll pull out your gray hairs.

517
00:32:24,226 --> 00:32:27,520
I have gray hairs? Why already?
That's so annoying.

518
00:32:32,067 --> 00:32:33,454
Why did you hit me?

519
00:32:33,456 --> 00:32:35,515
You nasty little thing.

520
00:32:35,973 --> 00:32:37,455
Why did you have to be a girl?

521
00:32:38,260 --> 00:32:41,727
If you were a boy, I'd beat you
three days straight and once more at dawn.

522
00:32:42,038 --> 00:32:43,087
Heung Sik.

523
00:32:43,112 --> 00:32:44,425
Is Gyu Rim a coffee cup?

524
00:32:44,875 --> 00:32:46,485
Is she a desk or a chair?

525
00:32:47,107 --> 00:32:49,801
Is she some object with no taste
and no thoughts of her own?

526
00:32:50,834 --> 00:32:53,330
Sim Cheong threw herself
into the sea for her father,

527
00:32:53,364 --> 00:32:55,027
and she can't do this much for her family?

528
00:32:55,554 --> 00:32:58,321
If she married you, we'd never have
to worry about a house again.

529
00:32:58,346 --> 00:33:00,250
Why does it have to be your sister?

530
00:33:01,181 --> 00:33:02,824
You be Sim Cheong, then.

531
00:33:02,826 --> 00:33:04,721
Then you'd never worry about a house.

532
00:33:05,262 --> 00:33:08,479
Leave your fiance and marry me
instead, then.

533
00:33:11,201 --> 00:33:12,601
Do you like me?

534
00:33:12,759 --> 00:33:14,149
Are you cursing me right now?

535
00:33:14,151 --> 00:33:15,752
Am I crazy?

536
00:33:15,777 --> 00:33:19,294
Right. You wouldn't take guys
like me by the truckload.

537
00:33:19,494 --> 00:33:22,946
And I wouldn't take a schemer like you
with a skyscraper thrown in.

538
00:33:25,261 --> 00:33:27,300
Every time you say something stupid,

539
00:33:27,301 --> 00:33:30,434
I'll tell your fiance
everything about your con.

540
00:33:31,381 --> 00:33:32,899
I ought to just kick you.

541
00:33:40,296 --> 00:33:41,610
I don't know.

542
00:33:41,889 --> 00:33:45,013
What do I care if they end up
on the street like beggars?

543
00:33:48,301 --> 00:33:52,161
Because it'll come back on me.

544
00:33:53,381 --> 00:33:56,907
What if they all come piling in,
begging me to save them?

545
00:33:59,633 --> 00:34:02,255
I have to get Han Gyu Rim
and Cho Heung Sik together somehow.

546
00:34:02,831 --> 00:34:05,038
But how?

547
00:34:13,994 --> 00:34:16,083
I'll eat this and build up my strength,

548
00:34:17,379 --> 00:34:21,294
and beat you somehow and get out,
just you watch.

549
00:34:25,581 --> 00:34:27,339
Every ten minutes that passes,

550
00:34:27,600 --> 00:34:29,987
I'll make things twice as hard
for your sister.

551
00:34:31,135 --> 00:34:34,673
The longer this drags on,
the worse it gets for your sister,

552
00:34:34,814 --> 00:34:37,447
so if you get it, move aside.

553
00:34:46,074 --> 00:34:48,576
Can't you just curse me
and hit me instead...

554
00:34:48,611 --> 00:34:50,447
until you cool down?

555
00:34:50,594 --> 00:34:52,260
Can't you go easy on my sister?

556
00:34:53,140 --> 00:34:55,734
I'd go easy if she wanted it.

557
00:34:56,820 --> 00:34:59,547
She says she'd sooner die
than take it back.

558
00:35:00,876 --> 00:35:04,547
I cared for her, I liked her so much...

559
00:35:06,841 --> 00:35:09,234
I'll hound her exactly as much
as I liked her.

560
00:35:09,547 --> 00:35:13,227
Exactly as much as I loved her.

561
00:35:14,635 --> 00:35:19,321
Hey, time just keeps ticking away.

562
00:35:20,020 --> 00:35:23,066
You think I can't ever get out of here?

563
00:35:24,541 --> 00:35:28,742
The more you and Heung Sik do this,
the harder it gets for your sister.

564
00:35:32,041 --> 00:35:33,041
Right.

565
00:35:33,531 --> 00:35:36,214
Blocking you like this
won't solve anything.

566
00:35:36,661 --> 00:35:37,978
That's right.

567
00:35:38,792 --> 00:35:40,447
Now we're talking.

568
00:35:45,054 --> 00:35:46,501
What are you doing?

569
00:35:56,384 --> 00:35:57,593
Hello, Gyu O.

570
00:35:58,154 --> 00:36:00,851
Gyu Rim, I'm at Heung Sik's place,

571
00:36:01,852 --> 00:36:04,607
I'm blocking Su Nam from going out.

572
00:36:05,114 --> 00:36:06,127
Why would you?

573
00:36:07,081 --> 00:36:09,420
In case she goes after you
and gives you a hard time.

574
00:36:11,267 --> 00:36:14,652
Don't, Gyu O. Don't block her.

575
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:16,746
This is my problem.

576
00:36:16,994 --> 00:36:19,720
I'm the one who did wrong,
and I'll fix it.

577
00:36:20,354 --> 00:36:21,720
Don't do that to her.

578
00:36:23,634 --> 00:36:26,634
Okay. You handle it, then.

579
00:36:27,987 --> 00:36:28,987
Well?

580
00:36:30,976 --> 00:36:34,987
Gyu Rim says not to block you.

581
00:36:36,161 --> 00:36:38,388
Your sister knows it too.

582
00:36:38,567 --> 00:36:40,488
The more you and Heung Sik do this,

583
00:36:40,490 --> 00:36:42,820
the more she's the one who suffers.

584
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:51,819
But Su Nam, why is the world
so unfair to Gyu Rim alone?

585
00:36:52,001 --> 00:36:53,267
What's unfair?

586
00:36:53,708 --> 00:36:57,592
Whenever something happens in our family,

587
00:36:57,594 --> 00:37:00,000
Gyu Rim solved it from start to finish,

588
00:37:02,120 --> 00:37:04,026
so why is there nothing...

589
00:37:05,503 --> 00:37:07,060
we can do for her?

590
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:14,677
No matter what you babble,

591
00:37:15,097 --> 00:37:17,627
I don't pity her one bit.

592
00:37:18,027 --> 00:37:20,170
If she made my child cry,

593
00:37:20,298 --> 00:37:23,914
she should weep blood. That's what's fair.

594
00:37:24,360 --> 00:37:26,053
I'm leaving. Good work.

595
00:37:26,174 --> 00:37:27,827
Eat this. It's delicious.

596
00:37:33,921 --> 00:37:36,216
Hello, Jeongin Mall, Unit 302?

597
00:37:36,490 --> 00:37:38,067
Yes, understood.

598
00:37:38,361 --> 00:37:41,027
We'll deliver within the hour. Thank you.

599
00:37:43,921 --> 00:37:46,341
Not scared at all, are you?

600
00:37:50,267 --> 00:37:51,300
You're here.

601
00:37:51,881 --> 00:37:55,385
No matter how much I give you a hard time,
you're not scared one bit.

602
00:37:55,387 --> 00:37:57,754
So you think you can take me on?

603
00:37:57,755 --> 00:37:59,406
No, Su Nam.

604
00:37:59,520 --> 00:38:01,527
Fine. Let's do this.

605
00:38:02,241 --> 00:38:06,026
You'll be the third to find out...

606
00:38:06,114 --> 00:38:08,534
just how ruthless I can be.

607
00:38:08,847 --> 00:38:12,595
The first one who crossed me...

608
00:38:12,597 --> 00:38:15,232
left the country because of me.

609
00:38:16,180 --> 00:38:17,940
The second one I went after...

610
00:38:18,241 --> 00:38:20,853
said prison was easier,

611
00:38:20,894 --> 00:38:23,574
and he's sitting in a cell right now.

612
00:38:26,167 --> 00:38:27,600
Where will you run to?

613
00:38:28,367 --> 00:38:30,027
Start thinking about it now.

614
00:38:34,279 --> 00:38:36,047
It's like a mouthful of salt.

615
00:38:36,361 --> 00:38:38,041
Why is this so salty?

616
00:38:45,801 --> 00:38:49,755
It tastes fine to me.

617
00:38:49,928 --> 00:38:52,565
Fine? Nothing about this is fine.

618
00:38:52,694 --> 00:38:57,417
Seasoning like this is why customers
don't buy what you make.

619
00:38:58,186 --> 00:39:01,506
I kept quiet all this time
so I wouldn't crush you,

620
00:39:02,234 --> 00:39:05,547
but those greens and side dishes you make,

621
00:39:05,614 --> 00:39:08,174
you'd be shocked how many complaints
there are.

622
00:39:08,647 --> 00:39:12,481
The kimchi I make gets nothing but praise.

623
00:39:13,374 --> 00:39:15,434
Every customer says the same thing,

624
00:39:15,654 --> 00:39:18,181
that they could do better themselves,

625
00:39:18,860 --> 00:39:24,051
and that I should have fired someone
this useless long ago.

626
00:39:27,349 --> 00:39:28,621
What's that look?

627
00:39:29,247 --> 00:39:32,174
You look like you think
you've been wronged.

628
00:39:33,061 --> 00:39:36,534
"My side dishes sell just fine."

629
00:39:36,721 --> 00:39:40,261
That look is arguing right back at me.

630
00:39:42,327 --> 00:39:43,820
If you feel wronged, leave.

631
00:39:44,020 --> 00:39:47,247
I won't stop you.
Write your resignation and go.

632
00:39:48,254 --> 00:39:49,302
I'm sorry.

633
00:39:49,603 --> 00:39:52,640
I'll be more careful from now on.

634
00:39:53,774 --> 00:39:55,255
What do you mean, from now on?

635
00:39:55,383 --> 00:39:57,068
You're getting fired soon anyway.

636
00:39:58,066 --> 00:40:01,384
And from now on,

637
00:40:02,619 --> 00:40:06,085
we're buying whole garlic, not peeled,

638
00:40:06,087 --> 00:40:08,707
so you'll peel every clove yourself.

639
00:40:11,187 --> 00:40:12,720
What, you can't peel it?

640
00:40:14,207 --> 00:40:16,381
I said, quit if you don't like it.

641
00:40:17,774 --> 00:40:19,254
No. I have no complaints.

642
00:40:19,481 --> 00:40:21,096
I'll peel all of it myself.

643
00:40:21,098 --> 00:40:22,460
Garlic. Whole garlic!

644
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:26,549
All right, then.

645
00:40:27,460 --> 00:40:30,635
- Order the whole garlic now.
- Yes.

646
00:40:48,680 --> 00:40:50,201
Is the bell broken?

647
00:40:51,213 --> 00:40:52,853
When did you come in, ma'am?

648
00:40:53,220 --> 00:40:56,127
You look like a first-time customer.

649
00:40:56,681 --> 00:41:00,140
We have plenty of good side dishes,
so take your time.

650
00:41:06,594 --> 00:41:08,640
Welcome. Have a look around.

651
00:41:09,327 --> 00:41:11,421
You didn't even know the bell was broken?

652
00:41:13,420 --> 00:41:14,920
It was fine this morning...

653
00:41:15,207 --> 00:41:18,076
What's gotten into you lately?

654
00:41:18,394 --> 00:41:20,727
I'll fix it right after
I get back from deliveries.

655
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:24,661
The more I dislike you, the more
you do to make it worse.

656
00:41:24,900 --> 00:41:26,401
I'll be back.

657
00:41:33,533 --> 00:41:37,454
Was that Han Gyu Rim who just walked out?

658
00:41:40,376 --> 00:41:43,620
Yes, it was. Why do you ask?

659
00:41:46,441 --> 00:41:48,602
The way you scolded her,

660
00:41:48,924 --> 00:41:51,127
she must have done something terrible.

661
00:41:51,974 --> 00:41:54,423
You're not here to buy side dishes.

662
00:41:54,698 --> 00:41:56,920
You came to see Han Gyu Rim?

663
00:41:57,881 --> 00:41:59,987
No, I came for side dishes.

664
00:42:00,967 --> 00:42:04,380
Could I try a sample of the kimchi?

665
00:42:04,787 --> 00:42:07,441
Of course. One moment.

666
00:42:13,242 --> 00:42:17,347
You make the kimchi yourself?

667
00:42:17,574 --> 00:42:19,981
I don't let anyone else make it.

668
00:42:20,321 --> 00:42:22,345
When it comes to kimchi,

669
00:42:22,370 --> 00:42:26,601
I take a back seat to nobody
in this country.

670
00:42:27,800 --> 00:42:29,040
Give it a taste.

671
00:42:35,767 --> 00:42:38,475
- Salty.
- Salty?

672
00:42:39,181 --> 00:42:40,861
That can't be right.

673
00:42:45,394 --> 00:42:47,318
What's salty about this?

674
00:42:47,321 --> 00:42:49,534
Are you arguing with me?

675
00:42:51,061 --> 00:42:53,927
- I'm not arguing,
- It's salty to me.

676
00:42:55,667 --> 00:42:58,040
You must eat everything bland.

677
00:42:58,387 --> 00:43:01,347
Then try this radish kimchi.

678
00:43:01,593 --> 00:43:05,218
I made this one mild for Seoul palates,

679
00:43:05,243 --> 00:43:08,344
so go ahead and try it.

680
00:43:15,427 --> 00:43:17,501
- Bitter.
- Bitter?

681
00:43:17,881 --> 00:43:20,127
You call this radish kimchi?

682
00:43:20,667 --> 00:43:22,980
I could make it better myself.

683
00:43:27,899 --> 00:43:29,066
Sour.

684
00:43:29,555 --> 00:43:32,027
How is green onion kimchi this sour?

685
00:43:32,029 --> 00:43:33,994
I wouldn't take this for free.

686
00:43:35,327 --> 00:43:37,060
Then don't buy it.

687
00:43:37,587 --> 00:43:40,285
I've got no intention of selling...

688
00:43:40,313 --> 00:43:42,507
to a customer like you, so leave.

689
00:43:43,827 --> 00:43:47,940
Thirty years in this business
and I've never heard anything like it.

690
00:43:48,797 --> 00:43:52,129
So I pay for it myself,

691
00:43:52,350 --> 00:43:54,361
and I can't even say it's too salty,
bitter, or sour?

692
00:43:54,467 --> 00:43:57,053
Your taste buds are the problem,

693
00:43:57,078 --> 00:43:59,256
so why blame my kimchi?

694
00:43:59,281 --> 00:44:02,027
Why do you have to disrespect me? Get out!

695
00:44:02,261 --> 00:44:03,578
I don't want a customer like you,

696
00:44:03,599 --> 00:44:07,150
even if you paid me by the sackful.
Get out!

697
00:44:07,419 --> 00:44:08,915
I said get out!

698
00:44:09,174 --> 00:44:11,489
What kind of place is this?

699
00:44:11,514 --> 00:44:14,948
- I'll report you!
- Go ahead!

700
00:44:14,973 --> 00:44:17,940
I'm not scared. Report me!

701
00:44:20,507 --> 00:44:22,391
You're not even from this neighborhood,

702
00:44:22,393 --> 00:44:25,441
so don't set foot around here again!

703
00:44:27,014 --> 00:44:28,927
That old hag, honestly!

704
00:44:30,361 --> 00:44:32,921
- Are you all right?
- Yes.

705
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:37,187
- Should I help you up?
- No, I'm fine.

706
00:44:43,351 --> 00:44:46,886
Is there a pharmacy around here,

707
00:44:47,447 --> 00:44:49,594
or maybe a convenience store?

708
00:44:50,640 --> 00:44:54,739
Go out to the arcade and turn right.
There's a rice cake shop. From there...

709
00:44:56,994 --> 00:44:58,340
Never mind, just follow me.

710
00:44:58,639 --> 00:45:01,818
- You can walk, right?
- Yes, of course.

711
00:45:06,141 --> 00:45:08,157
Of all the places she could work,

712
00:45:08,228 --> 00:45:11,134
why is she taking that kind of abuse
under that old hag?

713
00:45:12,707 --> 00:45:15,741
Han Gyu Rim, are you really that dense?

714
00:45:19,481 --> 00:45:21,946
There's a restroom behind the building.

715
00:45:22,401 --> 00:45:24,741
You can change your stockings there.

716
00:45:25,413 --> 00:45:27,740
Should I get you a pain patch
if you need one?

717
00:45:27,980 --> 00:45:30,596
No, this is plenty.

718
00:45:31,390 --> 00:45:33,604
- High school?
- Yes.

719
00:45:35,014 --> 00:45:37,627
You don't see students
like you these days.

720
00:45:37,740 --> 00:45:40,175
How did your parents raise you so well?

721
00:45:41,287 --> 00:45:43,880
If you don't need anything else,
I'll be going.

722
00:45:44,687 --> 00:45:47,451
Sure. I took up too much of your time.

723
00:45:47,899 --> 00:45:49,094
Hold on.

724
00:45:49,988 --> 00:45:51,274
This is all the cash I have.

725
00:45:51,276 --> 00:45:54,244
- Buy yourself something good.
- No, I'm fine.

726
00:45:54,611 --> 00:45:57,030
- Get well soon.
- Take it...

727
00:45:58,551 --> 00:45:59,634
Thank you.

728
00:46:02,653 --> 00:46:05,273
His mother must be bursting with pride.

729
00:46:07,467 --> 00:46:09,634
I'd love to have a son like that.

730
00:46:12,613 --> 00:46:14,500
Didn't that student leave this behind?

731
00:46:18,973 --> 00:46:21,327
Should I have at least asked his name?

732
00:46:26,859 --> 00:46:28,660
That crazy old hag!

733
00:46:28,987 --> 00:46:31,147
How do I get back at her?

734
00:46:34,647 --> 00:46:37,940
How do I get back at that crazy woman?

735
00:46:39,080 --> 00:46:40,961
The more I think about it,
the more it galls me.

736
00:46:41,723 --> 00:46:44,764
I can barely breathe from it.

737
00:46:46,126 --> 00:46:47,401
Su Nam.

738
00:46:49,394 --> 00:46:50,854
Your sister's not here. Go.

739
00:46:51,054 --> 00:46:53,281
I'm not here for her. I came to buy curry.

740
00:46:54,594 --> 00:46:56,221
You came to buy curry?

741
00:46:56,507 --> 00:46:58,994
I really wanted the curry Gyu Rim makes.

742
00:47:01,000 --> 00:47:04,514
Did your sister tell you to come
buy what she made?

743
00:47:05,234 --> 00:47:08,921
Just ask her to make it.
Why come all the way here?

744
00:47:08,946 --> 00:47:11,679
We decided everyone cooks
for themselves now.

745
00:47:13,720 --> 00:47:15,574
What's that supposed to mean?

746
00:47:15,607 --> 00:47:18,329
It means Gyu Rim stops worrying about us,

747
00:47:18,517 --> 00:47:20,940
eats what she wants, does what she wants,

748
00:47:21,481 --> 00:47:22,854
and lives that way from now on.

749
00:47:23,534 --> 00:47:25,840
How, all of a sudden?

750
00:47:27,068 --> 00:47:31,867
Because the person who matters most
to Gyu Rim is Gyu Rim herself.

751
00:47:33,011 --> 00:47:37,790
So what your sister did,

752
00:47:38,597 --> 00:47:40,566
as young people say these days,
is that she woke up?

753
00:47:41,973 --> 00:47:45,019
You're right.
I hadn't thought of it that way,

754
00:47:45,044 --> 00:47:47,316
but I think my sister woke up, Su Nam.

755
00:47:48,326 --> 00:47:50,062
You're the one who woke up, boy.

756
00:47:55,834 --> 00:47:59,226
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

757
00:47:59,385 --> 00:48:01,740
Where are you?

758
00:48:02,086 --> 00:48:03,817
Mu Jin!

759
00:48:04,172 --> 00:48:09,880
Where are you, Kim Mu Jin?

760
00:48:10,507 --> 00:48:15,233
Where are you, Kim Mu Jin?

761
00:48:15,413 --> 00:48:19,441
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

762
00:48:19,719 --> 00:48:26,354
Where are you, Mu Jin?

763
00:48:29,986 --> 00:48:34,486
Mu Jin.

764
00:48:34,807 --> 00:48:37,102
Kim Mu Jin.

765
00:48:37,584 --> 00:48:42,960
Where are you, Kim Mu Jin?

766
00:48:44,314 --> 00:48:46,387
Mu Jin.

767
00:48:46,425 --> 00:48:49,946
- Did you lose someone?
- My little brother.

768
00:48:51,940 --> 00:48:55,556
- How old is your brother?
- Nine.

769
00:48:56,414 --> 00:48:59,246
Where's your mom? Did you call the police?

770
00:48:59,539 --> 00:49:02,226
My mom's at work,

771
00:49:02,340 --> 00:49:06,566
and I was going to call
if I couldn't find him myself.

772
00:49:11,447 --> 00:49:13,468
Don't cry. It's okay.

773
00:49:13,493 --> 00:49:15,599
I'll help you look.

774
00:49:16,053 --> 00:49:17,663
What does Mu Jin look like?

775
00:49:17,774 --> 00:49:19,421
What color is he wearing today?

776
00:49:19,763 --> 00:49:22,413
Do you have a picture of him?

777
00:49:22,546 --> 00:49:24,960
I have a picture of Mu Jin.

778
00:49:37,767 --> 00:49:39,986
He's so cute, your Mu Jin.

779
00:49:40,673 --> 00:49:44,260
I'll look over there,
and you look that way.

780
00:49:44,861 --> 00:49:48,048
I'll put my number in, so save it,

781
00:49:48,189 --> 00:49:49,813
and we'll tell each other if we find him.

782
00:49:52,747 --> 00:49:54,137
Here.

783
00:49:55,219 --> 00:49:58,512
My name is Kim Mu Gyeong.

784
00:49:58,933 --> 00:50:02,889
All right, Mu Gyeong.
We'll find Mu Jin, I promise.

785
00:50:02,914 --> 00:50:04,265
Don't worry.

786
00:50:09,613 --> 00:50:13,645
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

787
00:50:15,483 --> 00:50:20,547
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

788
00:50:21,047 --> 00:50:24,653
Excuse me, have you seen
a puppy that looks like this?

789
00:50:25,153 --> 00:50:28,551
He's white, and his name is Mu Jin.

790
00:50:30,153 --> 00:50:34,268
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

791
00:50:36,840 --> 00:50:41,345
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

792
00:50:43,971 --> 00:50:48,005
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin!

793
00:50:48,274 --> 00:50:52,544
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin.

794
00:50:53,661 --> 00:50:59,369
Mu Jin. Kim Mu Jin!

795
00:51:04,274 --> 00:51:06,326
- Did you hear that?
- Hear what?

796
00:51:07,067 --> 00:51:08,626
Someone is calling my name.

797
00:51:08,651 --> 00:51:10,501
What are you talking about?

798
00:51:11,397 --> 00:51:13,366
I don't hear anything.

799
00:51:14,380 --> 00:51:15,813
She definitely called.

800
00:51:17,054 --> 00:51:19,534
Who? The Grim Reaper?

801
00:51:20,774 --> 00:51:22,820
No. Gyu Rim.

802
00:51:30,780 --> 00:51:33,214
I didn't sleep well last night.

803
00:51:34,154 --> 00:51:37,822
Sorry. I'll go splash
some cold water on my face.

804
00:51:42,961 --> 00:51:44,601
Make it ice water.

805
00:51:47,287 --> 00:51:48,634
Mu Jin.

806
00:51:51,246 --> 00:51:52,599
Kim Mu Jin.

807
00:51:55,234 --> 00:51:56,774
Mu Jin.

808
00:52:00,193 --> 00:52:01,820
Kim Mu Jin.

809
00:52:11,874 --> 00:52:13,880
Are you Mu Jin, by any chance?

810
00:52:20,347 --> 00:52:21,400
Come here.

811
00:52:21,734 --> 00:52:25,578
Your sister is going out of her mind
looking for you.

812
00:52:26,797 --> 00:52:30,015
Look at that. It is you.

813
00:52:31,181 --> 00:52:33,599
You really are Mu Jin.

814
00:52:37,887 --> 00:52:39,987
Found you, Kim Mu Jin.

815
00:52:43,066 --> 00:52:44,326
Found you.

816
00:52:55,860 --> 00:52:57,823
Pull yourself together, Kim Mu Jin.

817
00:52:57,848 --> 00:53:00,311
Come on. Pull it together.

818
00:53:23,214 --> 00:53:24,240
Yes?

819
00:53:25,020 --> 00:53:26,846
Is this Han Gyu O's phone?

820
00:53:27,934 --> 00:53:28,980
Who's asking?

821
00:53:30,034 --> 00:53:32,829
Hello. This is Min Ju,
Kwon Hui Na's friend.

822
00:53:34,042 --> 00:53:35,940
Yes, hello.

823
00:53:36,519 --> 00:53:39,366
I need to talk to you about Hui Na.

824
00:53:39,540 --> 00:53:41,426
Could we meet for a bit?

825
00:53:41,759 --> 00:53:43,741
Did something happen to Hui Na?

826
00:53:43,950 --> 00:53:45,200
Is she sick?

827
00:53:45,548 --> 00:53:47,347
I'll tell you in person.

828
00:54:01,114 --> 00:54:02,339
So what is it?

829
00:54:03,146 --> 00:54:05,826
- Have a seat first.
- Just tell me.

830
00:54:07,781 --> 00:54:10,034
Sit down, and I'll tell you.

831
00:54:18,448 --> 00:54:21,466
- What would you like?
- First, tell me what happened...

832
00:54:21,754 --> 00:54:23,234
to Hui Na.

833
00:54:28,927 --> 00:54:31,031
Nothing happened to Hui Na.

834
00:54:31,312 --> 00:54:33,013
I lied.

835
00:54:37,314 --> 00:54:39,954
You wouldn't have come if I'd asked.

836
00:54:44,920 --> 00:54:48,073
Hui Na says she isn't interested in you.

837
00:54:48,306 --> 00:54:50,159
That's why she didn't show up.

838
00:54:53,627 --> 00:54:54,946
Understood.

839
00:54:55,986 --> 00:54:59,846
She told me I should go for you.

840
00:55:03,227 --> 00:55:07,108
As far as I know,
you're Su Chan's girlfriend.

841
00:55:10,853 --> 00:55:13,040
I broke up with Su Chan a while ago.

842
00:55:13,454 --> 00:55:16,847
I can't stand two-timing.

843
00:55:20,534 --> 00:55:24,567
Stop chasing someone who doesn't want you.
Just date me instead.

844
00:55:24,947 --> 00:55:28,827
Date me, and you'll forget
someone like Kwon Hui Na fast.

845
00:55:32,081 --> 00:55:33,717
Sorry, but...

846
00:55:35,177 --> 00:55:38,740
I don't deal with lunatics
like you at all.

847
00:55:39,640 --> 00:55:42,509
Have an iced americano
with plenty of ice...

848
00:55:42,618 --> 00:55:44,080
and clear your head.

849
00:55:48,366 --> 00:55:49,873
Han Gyu O.

850
00:55:55,799 --> 00:55:59,679
Look at that. Sexier when he's angry.

851
00:56:01,381 --> 00:56:04,195
Now I definitely can't give him up.

852
00:56:20,867 --> 00:56:22,820
Min Ju really said that?

853
00:56:23,006 --> 00:56:25,506
That she'd break up with you
and date Han Gyu O?

854
00:56:25,613 --> 00:56:28,053
She said she told you too.

855
00:56:28,240 --> 00:56:29,713
That little...

856
00:56:30,227 --> 00:56:31,850
Is she out of her mind?

857
00:56:35,167 --> 00:56:37,265
We think she's crazy,

858
00:56:37,959 --> 00:56:40,127
but Min Ju doesn't think she is.

859
00:56:40,261 --> 00:56:42,531
She thinks she's just being
honest about her feelings.

860
00:56:42,556 --> 00:56:44,728
Still, does this make any sense?

861
00:56:48,359 --> 00:56:49,921
I'm the crazy one.

862
00:56:49,921 --> 00:56:52,141
I'm the one who introduced her
to Han Gyu O.

863
00:56:52,166 --> 00:56:54,894
How could you be so shortsighted?

864
00:56:54,919 --> 00:56:56,960
Seo Min Ju is famous
for falling for a pretty face,

865
00:56:56,985 --> 00:56:58,740
and you didn't see her losing it?

866
00:56:58,765 --> 00:57:03,605
Han Gyu O is so gorgeous
that grandmothers turn around for him,

867
00:57:03,724 --> 00:57:06,727
and you dangled him in front of her?

868
00:57:06,752 --> 00:57:09,023
You've been around Seo Min Ju that long
and missed that,

869
00:57:09,025 --> 00:57:11,520
and now you cause this much trouble?

870
00:57:11,721 --> 00:57:13,889
I just...

871
00:57:15,081 --> 00:57:18,440
wanted to bring Gyu O and you together...

872
00:57:20,120 --> 00:57:23,314
I assumed you liked
Gyu O too, obviously...

873
00:57:23,947 --> 00:57:26,687
So is that my fault?

874
00:57:27,473 --> 00:57:29,374
Then why is Han Gyu O not good enough?

875
00:57:29,567 --> 00:57:33,300
Like you said, he's gorgeous,
he's cool, he's full of charm,

876
00:57:33,387 --> 00:57:35,763
and honestly, if you just liked Gyu O,

877
00:57:35,788 --> 00:57:37,600
everything would be solved.

878
00:57:38,333 --> 00:57:42,826
Aren't you the one causing trouble here?

879
00:58:07,379 --> 00:58:10,166
(Mu Gyeong)

880
00:58:10,367 --> 00:58:13,527
Hi there, Mu Jin.

881
00:58:13,552 --> 00:58:17,752
Thanks to you, my Mu Jin
is safe and sound.

882
00:58:17,854 --> 00:58:20,814
That's a relief. Such a relief.

883
00:58:20,981 --> 00:58:24,427
Mu Jin, say thank you to the nice lady.

884
00:58:24,787 --> 00:58:27,602
Mu Jin, don't get lost again,

885
00:58:27,627 --> 00:58:30,427
and be happy with your mom and sister.

886
00:58:30,452 --> 00:58:33,804
Thank you. Bye.

887
00:58:33,853 --> 00:58:35,606
Bye, Mu Gyeong.

888
00:58:36,371 --> 00:58:39,491
Bye, Kim Mu Jin.

889
00:58:45,460 --> 00:58:47,174
Thank you, Kim Mu Jin.

890
00:58:48,075 --> 00:58:50,827
Thanks to you, I got to say
that name a whole lot.

891
00:59:11,954 --> 00:59:13,413
I can't take it.

892
00:59:15,047 --> 00:59:17,574
Even if I'm cursed for it, I can't.

893
00:59:33,520 --> 00:59:34,790
Welcome.

894
00:59:35,244 --> 00:59:38,258
- Are you here to eat?
- Yes.

895
00:59:42,652 --> 00:59:44,015
Go on with your work.

896
00:59:46,120 --> 00:59:48,260
What brings you here?

897
00:59:48,447 --> 00:59:51,287
Mu Jin is extremely busy right now.

898
00:59:54,634 --> 00:59:56,460
I came to eat.

899
00:59:57,420 --> 00:59:58,433
Sorry?

900
01:00:01,780 --> 01:00:03,720
This is a restaurant, isn't it?

901
01:00:07,246 --> 01:00:08,389
It is.

902
01:00:09,765 --> 01:00:12,381
Have a seat over there, then.

903
01:00:22,113 --> 01:00:23,893
Here's the menu.

904
01:00:31,767 --> 01:00:33,533
Kimchi fried rice, please.

905
01:00:35,600 --> 01:00:38,513
We don't have kimchi fried rice
on our menu.

906
01:01:03,911 --> 01:01:07,220
Can you do kimchi fried rice?

907
01:01:08,106 --> 01:01:10,073
Kimchi fried rice, out of nowhere?

908
01:01:14,013 --> 01:01:15,053
You can't, right?

909
01:01:15,454 --> 01:01:16,874
I'll make it for you at home.

910
01:01:17,293 --> 01:01:20,493
Forget home. A customer wants it.

911
01:01:21,527 --> 01:01:23,634
Tell them to order from the menu.

912
01:01:23,680 --> 01:01:25,206
I already did.

913
01:01:27,788 --> 01:01:29,307
Who's the customer?

914
01:01:34,753 --> 01:01:35,926
An elderly person?

915
01:01:39,420 --> 01:01:41,640
Not elderly, no.

916
01:01:42,214 --> 01:01:43,876
Then he should order from the menu.

917
01:01:54,867 --> 01:01:56,367
What is it?

918
01:01:58,500 --> 01:01:59,706
Something's going on, isn't it?

919
01:02:00,233 --> 01:02:01,824
Why am I so soft?

920
01:02:01,849 --> 01:02:03,950
Especially with children, women,
and the elderly.

921
01:02:04,360 --> 01:02:06,773
Who ordered the kimchi fried rice?

922
01:02:07,434 --> 01:02:08,480
A child?

923
01:02:10,600 --> 01:02:11,740
A woman?

924
01:02:12,907 --> 01:02:14,581
Your type of woman again?

925
01:02:17,140 --> 01:02:19,246
Tell her to order from the menu.

926
01:02:19,612 --> 01:02:23,912
Or go ask, "You're my type.
Want kimchi fried rice with me?"

927
01:02:23,937 --> 01:02:25,550
Make the offer yourself.

928
01:02:28,227 --> 01:02:30,934
The woman who's very much my type
is named Han Gyu Rim.

929
01:02:33,500 --> 01:02:37,070
I'm not saying date her again.
One bowl of kimchi fried rice,

930
01:02:37,764 --> 01:02:39,173
you can do that much, can't you?

931
01:04:27,220 --> 01:04:29,470
- There's kimchi in the fridge, right?
- Yes.

932
01:04:57,000 --> 01:04:59,327
(Love on the Menu)

933
01:04:59,434 --> 01:05:02,675
Forget your wedding.
Call the whole thing off.

934
01:05:02,700 --> 01:05:04,334
No matter what happens, I'm marrying him.

935
01:05:04,367 --> 01:05:06,691
That girl Mu Jin dated,

936
01:05:06,807 --> 01:05:09,566
she's my daughter.

937
01:05:10,374 --> 01:05:13,225
What's wrong? Were you crying?

938
01:05:13,250 --> 01:05:16,083
My mom is type O, but I'm type AB.

939
01:05:16,108 --> 01:05:17,679
Gyeol, where are you?

940
01:05:17,704 --> 01:05:18,819
This is Kim Mu Jin.

941
01:05:19,213 --> 01:05:21,999
Then who is my mom?

942
01:05:22,534 --> 01:05:25,354
And who is my dad?

943
01:05:26,802 --> 01:05:28,602
Dramaday.me
